# Verification is the control (never a claim without proof)

- Schema/columns/enums/tables → verify on the Neon PROD branch `br-fancy-credit-akjnd07a` (`information_schema`/`pg_catalog`), NOT memory, migration files, or docs. Prod has diverged from migrations repeatedly — **prod wins**.
- **RLS 0-COUNT LANDMINE (mandatory):** `catalogs.*`, `mdata.*`, `accounting.*`, `banking.*`, `lib.*` are FORCED-RLS. A `0` is NOT a verdict. Re-run in the SAME transaction after `SELECT set_config('app.bypass_rls','lucia',true)` (or `SET app.operating_company_id`). A masked 0 has already caused false "gap" findings — always re-run before concluding.
- A migration can be **ledgered but ineffective** (its precondition/`WHERE NOT EXISTS` skipped). Verify the EFFECT (row/column/policy exists), not just the ledger entry.
- CI-green ≠ done. Merged ≠ done. Deployed ≠ live until `/api/v1/healthz/shallow` `version` == merge SHA.
- Definition of done = `acceptance[]` resolves on live evidence (file + route mounted + migration on prod + column populated 0-NULL + guard wired + planted-failure proof + browser/endpoint confirm). Cannot verify → say "UNVERIFIED", never guess.
- `ih35_app` CANNOT run DDL. Build+validate migrations on a throwaway Postgres (apply-twice, idempotent); the OWNER applies on Neon + ledger-backfills; GUARD re-proves live with the RLS bypass.
